        '【Content of a human-dao lineage-holder friend】',
        'Most people enjoy reading dan scriptures and awakening on their own — in truth not self-awakening but self-delusion. Think: since ancient times the dharma is not passed to six ears; would they truly write the crucial things into dan scriptures? And leave it at a word like “voidness” and done? Leave aside whether the dan scriptures are true or false, what attainment their authors had, whether the attribution is a borrowed name — even when an accomplished one writes secret texts to pass down to disciples’ disciples, outsiders who take them gain little, for many things are told mouth to ear, and the written formulas exist only as memoranda. So one without a lineage — unless he too spends the efforts and sacrifices of many generations attempting it — can almost never, by self-awakening, obtain true dao-methods. If you must read books, do not read the dan scriptures; read the root classics of the Daoist school — the Daode, the Nanhua and the like — and that is enough.',
