        '【Content of a human-dao lineage-holder friend】',
        'The great Dao: heaven and earth evolve naturally; where there is life there is death. When a person dies it is as a lamp snuffed out; if one does not cultivate to be true with the Dao, one cannot but scatter into ash and smoke — and who would administer this reincarnation? The Dao has no good or evil; good and evil exist only in the human heart — and then by whose standard are good and evil judged, how is this karma calculated, and who carries out the retribution?',
        'The six paths of rebirth and karmic retribution are Brahmanical ideas; Buddhism inherited them and carried them east, and they belong within divine-way systems. There is no such thing as one eternal, undying soul endlessly reincarnating. The objective causal connections among things cannot be denied — but a karmic retribution cycling through lives according to good and evil does not exist. Or rather, such things exist only within the Buddha-realm; they are not universal truth between heaven and earth.',
