        'This counts as one test. Now let us examine it closely.',
        'For an ordinary person in that woman’s place — how many could eat it? Don’t tell me she could — that is because you have seen the whole thing complete; the one standing aside talking does not feel his back ache.',
        'Plainly put: how many could bear humiliation of such degree?',
        'And after bearing it, finding nothing changed at all — how many would not rage, not resent, not fly into hysterics?',
        'Few, right?',
        'Here someone may say: isn’t this, damn it, just humiliation?',
        'Ah — correct; among tests there may indeed be an item of humiliation.',
        'A true test you cannot imagine beforehand: perhaps certain matters, perhaps certain views, perhaps deliberate humiliation, perhaps even your every word and act — and so on!!!',
        'Now look: how many could pass?!',
        'Here one may say: if it means passing such things, damn it, I want no part of this cultivation!!!',
        'Ah — congratulations!!!',
        'Successfully filtered out.',
        'You may rage, may shrug, may curse aloud — but this is reality!!!',
        'The examples above are complete ones; now suppose some incomplete ones.',
        'For example: you are male; I tell you henceforth never to approach sex — how many pass? 【Not even speaking of abstaining from sex: how many, damn it, cannot even quit jerking off — and still talk of cultivation…】',
        'For example: a bowl of shit is held out for you to eat — how many manage it?',
        'For example: you are a pretty girl, and I want to bed you — how many can go through with it?',
        'Here one may say: if it means passing such things, damn it, I want no part of this cultivation!!!',
        'Ah — congratulations!!!',
        'Successfully filtered out.',
        'You may rage, may shrug, may curse aloud — but this is reality!!!',
        'Whether the examples above, or the rumored “kill the wife to prove the Way,” or cutting off an arm as offering to Buddha, or whatever abstinence, eating shit, sleeping attendance and so on, or other things — most tests are every possible means of elimination, of finishing people off — even utterly extreme, against human nature, against feeling, against cognition, against the three views — such things; how many could pass?!!!',
        'Of course, within these situations there are deliberate obstructions: for instance, some person was found out, hounded unbearably by fawning dogs, and one does not wish to take them — and so on; there may be deliberate hard treatment.',
        'Of course, there are also tests extremely simple — simple as a mere formality.',
        'And so on and so on — every kind of situation, all-encompassing. In one word: even meeting the real, few can pass; and what seems to be one matter contains many matters — for instance, obedience.',
        'If you do not even obey — why would I take you?',
        'If you do not obey, and even taken, in ordinary teaching you talk back once, twice, extrapolate a third time — why keep you? To find myself discomfort?',
        'Why do masters sometimes like to take children as disciples, or those obedient in this respect?',
        'Because they are blank paper — easy to teach.',
        'Once a thing has its own notions in someone, correcting them is painstaking and laborious — and troublesome; and if the other then extrapolates — who the hell still teaches such goods? 【I, at least, do not teach them — this effort, would it not be sweeter spent raising a new one? Don’t look at me like this — basically any cultivator is like this.】',
        'Second, if this person does not obey, then very likely in practice they will not walk honestly either; then trouble is only a matter of time. I toil to raise a person, and because of disobedience they end in trouble — with that time, would I not rather raise an obedient one?',
        'Second, a rigid fierce sense of notions must also be broken — a point especially so for women.',
        'Imagine: you toil to raise a disciple; her practice is quite good — then because of some matter some day, she loses her chastity, and then cries, makes scenes, attempts suicide; or collapses from then on — tell me, raising her so long with such effort, for what? Harsh words, but reality is just so.',
        'Because her notions, her cognition, were kidnapped by a bit of traditional thinking — in this point even a prostitute is more transparent!!!',
        'Speaking of this, I cannot help but improvise a complaint: in cultivation, besides methods and practice, many things must also be broken through — and this is often one reason most beings cannot pass the tests.',
        '【Second, many beings after crossing the gate meet with phenomena hard to accept — say nothing of cultivators, speak of certain religions or dharma-sects: for example, after crossing the gate, when receiving qi, drinking others’ spittle and such. Of course, whether the person himself knows — that is his own affair; much more will not be said — see the example as an example.】',
        'So — through all, all, everything, in the end it comes down to the individual’s resolve in seeking the Way, nothing more!!!!',
