        'Are matter and consciousness necessarily different?? Necessarily two things?? All things do not leave yin and yang: the pole of matter is consciousness, the pole of consciousness is matter; the two are the embrace of yin and yang — to cultivate consciousness alone, the solitary yin does not grow. Only in cultivating both nature and life can body and spirit not separate, spirit and form both wondrous. To cultivate to earth-immortal, even to transcend this heaven and earth, understanding of matter is indispensable; though not limited to matter, only by first being able to master matter can one avoid being limited by matter.',
